  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "No chapter describes the hall’s architecture beyond naming it as the place of that conference.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the Central Great Hall, Duke Long and Fairy Zi Wei converse about Longevity Heaven’s attack and the qi wall’s exposed weaknesses. Fairy Zi Wei lists three Demon Venerable paths: Limitless Demon Venerable’s left path passes Five Deity Hall then Central Great Hall among other sites; Reckless Savage Demon Venerable’s central path and Red Lotus Demon Venerable’s right path each also pass Central Great Hall before ending at Heaven Overseeing Tower.",
      "chapters": [
        1710
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_duke_long",
        "char_fairy_zi_wei",
        "fac_longevity_heaven",
        "char_limitless_demon_venerable",
        "loc_five_deity_hall",
        "char_reckless_savage_demon_venerable",
        "char_red_lotus_demon_venerable",
        "house_heaven_overseeing_tower"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Central Great Hall is the control area of all the Immortal Gu Houses, and Fairy Zi Wei is in charge of it. From there she knows the refinement path formation’s progress and answers Duke Long that fate Gu needs six hours more. Even so, the hall has low defense: Heavenly Court did not expect enemies to attack it. It was once attacked by three Demon Venerables and even destroyed, yet Heavenly Court’s Gu Immortals did not reinforce its defense later, because against a venerable no defense would matter. Fairy Zi Wei reads the true flaw as mindset rather than walls. Calamity Luck Altar charges down at the hall; if it hit, the entire Central Great Hall would be reduced to shambles, until Duke Long stops the Immortal Gu House midair.",
      "chapters": [
        1713
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "control-hub",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "gu_fate_gu",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "house_calamity_luck_altar"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After the hall falls, Fairy Zi Wei’s control of Heavenly Court’s palaces drops drastically, and she would need much time and effort to mobilize them. The Central Great Hall becomes a pile of rubbles, with Heaven Overseeing Tower ahead of Calamity Luck Altar. An awakened Heavenly Court Gu Immortal notes that Central Great Hall was destroyed.",
      "chapters": [
        1715
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "destroyed-control-seat",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heavenly Court, Central Great Hall: Fairy Zi Wei sits in her usual seat, radiating intense purple light that fills the hall as she counters Fang Yuan’s wisdom path defenses and summons Star Constellation Chessboard.",
      "chapters": [
        1762
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "deduction-seat",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "house_star_constellation_chessboard"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Central Great Hall is finally repaired, and Qin Ding Ling is the person taking charge. Heavenly Court failed to repair fate Gu, suffered huge battle damage, and many areas are still in ruins even then.",
      "chapters": [
        1970
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "repair-and-new-charge",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_qin_ding_ling"
      ]
    }
